---
import "@styles/global.module.css";
import Header from "@components/header.astro";
import Scripts from "@components/scripts.astro";
import Footer from "@components/footer.astro";
import Meta from "@components/meta.astro";
import Cursor from "@components/cursor.astro";
import Tabs from "@components/Tabs.astro";
import Tab from "@components/Tab.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <style>
            .warning {
                background-color: rgb(75, 75, 0);
                padding: 0.5em;
                margin: 0.5em;
                border: 2px solid gray;
                border-top: 2px solid lightgray;
                border-left: 2px solid lightgray;
            }
        </style>
        <Meta name="Akabot" description="A Discord bot by Lunya" />
        <Scripts />
        <Cursor />
    </head>

    <body>
        <canvas id="background"></canvas>

        <!-- God damnit, I'm forced to use inline styles because Astro is stupid -->
        <div style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;">
            <Header />
            <main>
                <h1>Akabot</h1>
                <Tabs>
                    <Tab href="/project/akabot" selected>About</Tab>
                    <Tab href="/project/akabot/privacy">Privacy Policy</Tab>
                    <Tab href="/project/akabot/tos">Terms of Service</Tab>
                </Tabs>
                <p>A verified Discord bot by Lunya, filled to the brim with cool features, all for free of charge.</p>

                <div>
                    <a href="https://discord.com/discovery/applications/1172922944033411243">
                        <button>Invite</button>
                    </a>
                    <a href="https://discord.gg/YFksXpXnn6">
                        <button>Support Discord</button>
                    </a>
                    <a href="https://git.lunya.pet/Lunya/Akabot">
                        <button>Forgejo (Lunya's instance)</button>
                    </a>
                    <a href="https://codeberg.org/Akabot/Akabot">
                        <button>Codeberg</button>
                    </a>
                </div>

                <p>This Discord bot provides numerous features to enrich your server experience. Below is a simple explanation of what this bot offers:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Anti Raid - The Antiraid module prevents way too many joins in a short period of time.</li>
                    <li>Automod Actions - Create automod actions for specific rules executing specific actions and perform tasks when a member triggers an automod rule.</li>
                    <li>Anonymous Quefessions - Have people send you anonymous quefessions in your Discord server, with moderation abilities.</li>
                    <li>Auto React - React to messages automatically on a keyword.</li>
                    <li>Auto Response - Respond with a message automatically on a keyword.</li>
                    <li>Chat Revive - The Chat Revive commands revives commands if there&#39;s no seen activity for a set period of time.</li>
                    <li>Chat Streaks - The Chat Streaks module counts how many days you&#39;ve sent a message consecutively in a Discord server.</li>
                    <li>Chat Summary - The chat summary module counts messages and then sends a message at the end of the day.</li>
                    <li>Economy - This module introduces an economy system to Akabot, allowing users to earn, spend, and manage virtual currency within their Discord server.</li>
                    <li>Giveaways - The Giveaways module allows server administrators to create and manage giveaways directly within their Discord server.</li>
                    <li>Heartbeat - Configure the bot to send messages to another server on intervals to let the server know it&#39;s alive and online.</li>
                    <li>Help - Get help with the bot directly from the bot! Will direct you to a wiki anyone can contribute to.</li>
                    <li>Leveling - The Leveling module allows server administrators to implement and manage a leveling system within their Discord server.</li>
                    <li>Logging - This module adds logging for a Discord server. It sends events into a logging channel.</li>
                    <li>Message Time Capsule - This module allows users to schedule messages, reminders, and collection messages in Discord servers and DMs.</li>
                    <li>Moderation - This module provides commands to perform moderation actions such as kicking, banning, timing out, and removing timeouts for users in a Discord server.</li>
                    <li>
                        Reaction Roles - This module allows users to assign or remove roles by reacting to messages containing specific buttons. It provides commands to create different types of reaction role setups, such as normal,
                        add-only, remove-only, and single-choice reaction roles.
                    </li>
                    <li>Roles on Join - Give members roles immediately on join.</li>
                    <li>Send Server Count - Admins can configure the bot to send messages to top.gg and various other sites to update the server count.</li>
                    <li>
                        Suggestions - Akabot accepts suggestions directly from the bot! Using the public instance
                        <code>/suggest</code> command will create issues here.
                    </li>
                    <li>Statistics Channels - Channels that display various server statistics.</li>
                    <li>Temporary Voice Channels - Create as many voice channels in your Discord server without needing to ask admins to create them for you.</li>
                    <li>Tickets - Handle tickets in your Discord server. Let members open tickets, get help and close tickets. Comes with an auto close feature and archive feature.</li>
                    <li>Verification - This module adds user verification in Discord servers. It prevents bots from accessing your Discord server.</li>
                    <li>Welcome and Goodbye messages - Welcome new members, and say goodbye to the ones who leave.</li>
                    <li>Word Scramble - Scrambles random English words or words from previous messagse in chat and lets your members unscramble them for extra rewards in the leveling system.</li>
                </ul>

                <p>The bot has all of these features while being fully free and open source without any limitations.</p>

                <p>
                    If you think that any features are missing from the bot, you can suggest them straight from the bot using
                    <code>/feedback suggest</code>. They will be added if they're good.
                </p>
            </main>
            <Footer />
        </div>
        <script is:inline defer src="/scripts/background.js"></script>
    </body>
</html>
